› The goal here is to first work on canonicalization. We'll be simultaneously improving diff_engine.mm2 and diff_engine_fused.mm2 as they are alternate implementations attempting to
  accomplish the same thing (and return identical results).

  What we need to do is to make things more efficient, using the architecture and design of MORK by moving all numbers to the left-hand side of our expressions as we process through the
  computations and pattern matches.

  Currently there is wasted effort by not doing that. Please rewrite both mm2 files (or only 1 if appropriate?) to complete the refactor I'm asking for.


• I’m treating “numbers on the left” as a canonical-form invariant for the commutative constructors add and mul: numeric–numeric terms still fold, expression–numeric terms are rewritten to
  numeric–expression, and downstream rules only need the canonical orientation. I’ll trace every construction site before editing so the post-process and fused paths remain semantically
  aligned and their result sets stay identical.

