• The construction trace shows one important boundary: diff_engine.mm2 deliberately emits unsimplified symbolic trees and cannot know whether $du/$dv will be numeric from syntax alone.
  Canonicalization belongs in its companion simplify.mm2; the alternate fused engine has the same smart-constructor layer internally. I’m therefore changing those two equivalent
  construction layers, while documenting in the plain engine why it delegates this invariant instead of duplicating classification machinery.

• The environment’s patch helper is failing at sandbox startup (bwrap: loopback: Failed RTM_NEWADDR) even under the approved elevated execution path. I’m continuing with the system patch
  utility for the same scoped unified diff; the user-owned instruction file remains untouched.

